  "upload_type": "software",
  "title": "RISE Humanities Data Benchmark",
  "description": "<p>The RISE Humanities Data Benchmark, maintained by RISE (Research and Infrastructure Support) at the University of Basel, evaluates large language models on tasks from humanities research: transcribing, interpreting and extracting structured data from historical documents such as letters, library cards, newspaper advertisements and medieval manuscripts, scored against ground truths defined by domain experts, with the cost and runtime of every request.</p><p>The software contains the benchmarks (images and texts, prompts, answer schemas, ground truths and scorers, each described in a benchmark card with its version history), the test configurations, the runner that queries the models through one interface for all providers and scores their answers, and every stored result.</p><p>The stored results are also published as a dataset of joinable tables, one release per software release: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23821532\">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23821532</a>. The results are compared on <a href=\"https://rise-services.rise.unibas.ch/benchmarks/\">https://rise-services.rise.unibas.ch/benchmarks/</a>.</p>",
